  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Baby, tell me, what's your motive? (Motive) \n\nWhat's your motive? \n\nWhat's your motive? (Ah) \n\nSo tell me, what's your motive? (What's your motive?)\n\nYou are given an array AAA consisting of NNN positive integers.\n\nIn one operation, you have to:\n\n\nCalculate the lcm and gcd of the array;\nMultiply each element of the array by the calculated lcm, and divide each element of the array by the calculated gcd.\nFormally, let AXA^{X}AX be the array after performing XXX operations, where A0=AA^{0} = AA0=A.\n\nLet GGG denote the gcd of A(X−1)A^{(X - 1)}A(X−1) and LLL denote the lcm of A(X−1)A^{(X - 1)}A(X−1).\n\nThen, AX=A(X−1)⋅LG=[A1(X−1)⋅LG,A2(X−1)⋅LG,…,AN(X−1)⋅LG]A^{X} = A^{(X - 1)} \\cdot \\frac{L}{G} = [A^{(X - 1)}_1 \\cdot \\frac{L}{G}, A^{(X - 1)}_2 \\cdot \\frac{L}{G}, \\ldots, A^{(X - 1)}_N \\cdot \\frac{L}{G}]AX=A(X−1)⋅GL​=[A1(X−1)​⋅GL​,A2(X−1)​⋅GL​,…,AN(X−1)​⋅GL​].\n\nYou are given QQQ queries. Each query is represented an integer KKK.\n\nFind the gcd and lcm of AKA^{K}AK modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line will contain a single integer NNN, denoting the number of integers in AAA.\nThe second line will contain NNN positive integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the integers in AAA.\nThe third line will contain a single integer QQQ, denoting the number of queries.\nThe next QQQ lines each will contain a single integer KKK, denoting the number of operations to perform.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, output the gcd and lcm of AKA^{K}AK, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1071 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^71≤Ai​≤107",
      "1≤Q≤1051 \\leq Q \\leq 10^51≤Q≤105",
      "0≤K≤1090 \\leq K \\leq 10^90≤K≤109"
    ],
